    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Jesus Jones’ Twilight is the band’s eighth studio album, arriving after an eight-year gap and presented as a fresh chapter rather than a nostalgia exercise. Built around the group’s long-standing blend of electronic textures and driving rock, it preserves the propulsive, dance-inflected energy that helped define their sound while leaning into more reflective, expansive songwriting. The album’s rollout highlighted tracks like “Shot in the Chevy” and “Bad Zoo Rescue,” underscoring a record that balances hooks, atmosphere, and restless momentum.\n\nAs a late-career statement, Twilight reflects a band still interested in reinvention without abandoning its core identity. Its material has been described as exploring change, resilience, memory, and modern life, which fits Jesus Jones’ history of fusing sharp pop instincts with a club-oriented sense of rhythm. Released on Bucks Music, the album continues their tradition of making electronic rock feel both immediate and widescreen.",
